  summary: "The Western Roman Empire fell in 476 AD under Germanic invasions and internal decline, leaving the Roman Christian church as the main civilizing force in Western Europe. The Eastern Roman (Byzantine) Empire survived because it was richer and better defended, reached its height under Justinian I, produced the Justinian Code and Hagia Sophia, and preserved Greek learning and Roman law until 1453. In the West, the Frankish kingdom of Charles Martel and Charlemagne briefly reunited much of the old empire and was crowned by the pope in 800 AD.",
