      given: "Serfs could not leave the manor without the lord's permission and owed unpaid labour and dues, but they could not be forced off the manor, kept land for their own family and received protection.",
      formula: "Framework: compare a historical status against a definition before applying a label to it.",
      substitution: "A slave is property who can be sold and driven off at will; a serf was tied to the land but had recognised rights and protection.",
