  summary: "Islam arose in Arabia in the 7th century AD, and after the Hijira of 622 AD it spread with remarkable speed under the caliphs, producing the Umayyad and Abbasid empires and a golden age of learning between about 800 and 1200 AD. The Ottoman Turks built the greatest Muslim state, taking Constantinople in 1453 and reaching their height under Suleiman I before declining after 1566. In China the dynastic cycle of the Mandate of Heaven shaped the rise and fall of dynasties, and the Tang and Song periods brought prosperity and inventions such as gunpowder, the compass and movable type printing.",
