      given: "The Council of Trent (1545-1563) redefined Catholic beliefs and ended the sale of indulgences, but the church also banned Protestant books and established the Inquisition.",
      formula: "Framework: judge a movement by both what it corrected and what it resisted.",
      substitution: "Ending indulgences and redefining beliefs addressed real abuses, while the Inquisition and book bans tried to stop Protestantism by force.",
      calculation: "Because it both corrected abuses and used coercion, the Counter Reformation was reform and reaction at the same time.",
