  summary: "Between about 1500 and 1700 the Scientific Revolution replaced accepted theories with knowledge based on observation, experiment and reasoning, as Copernicus proposed a sun-centred universe, Galileo used the telescope and was punished in 1633, and Newton explained all motion through the law of universal gravitation. New instruments such as the microscope, barometer and thermometer, and work in medicine by Vesalius, Jenner and Boyle, expanded knowledge. In the 1700s the Enlightenment, or Age of Reason, applied the same trust in reason to society through the five ideas of reason, nature, happiness, progress and liberty, and thinkers such as Locke, Montesquieu, Voltaire, Beccaria and Wollstonecraft shaped modern ideas of rights, government and equality.",
